\v 5 But \nd Yeshua¦63950\nd* continued, “\wj Honestly, I'm¦63953 telling¦63953 you¦63954: unless a person is¦63958 born¦63958 from both water¦63961 \+em and¦63962\+em* the \+nd spirit¦63963\+nd*, they can't¦63965 enter¦63967 \nd God's¦63974\nd* kingdom¦63971.\wj*
\v 6 \wj Someone that's born¦63978 from a body¦63982 is¦63984 flesh¦63983 \+add and bone\+add*, but¦63985 someone that's born¦63987 from \+add &God's¦63989\+add* \+nd spirit¦63990\+nd* is¦63992 spiritual¦63991.\wj*
\v 7 \wj So you¦63994 shouldn't¦63993 be surprised that¦63995 I¦63996 told¦63996 you¦63997 that everyone¦64000 needs to¦64002 be¦64002 reborn.\wj*
\v 8 \wj The¦64004 wind blows¦64008 wherever¦64006 it wants¦64007, and¦64009 you¦64013 can hear¦64013 its¦64012 sound¦64011 but¦64014 you¦64016 can't¦64015 \+add actually\+add* see where¦64017 it's¦64018 coming¦64018 from or where¦64021 it's¦64022 going¦64022 to. So¦64023 too with everyone¦64025 who's born¦64027 from \+add &God's¦64032\+add* \+nd spirit¦64033\+nd*.\wj*”
\p
\v 9 Nicodemus¦64035 replied, “How¦64039 can all that even happen¦64042?”
\p
\v 10 “\wj You're¦64058 a Jewish teacher¦64052,\wj*” \nd Yeshua¦64045\nd* answered¦64043, “\wj and¦64046 yet you¦64049 don't¦64057 know¦64058 all that?\wj*
\v 11 \wj It's true that¦64063 we¦64066 just teach what¦64064 we¦64065 know¦64065, and¦64067 explain what¦64068 we've¦64069 seen¦64069 ourselves, but¦64071 you¦64077 people aren't¦64076 accepting¦64077 our¦64074 testimony¦64073.\wj*
\v 12 \wj If¦64078 I¦64081 tell¦64081 all of you earthly¦64080 \+add >things\+add* and¦64084 you¦64086 don't¦64085 believe¦64086 them, how¦64088 will¦64094 you ever believe¦64094 if¦64089 I¦64090 explain \+em heavenly¦64093\+em* \+add >things\+add* \+add to you\+add*?\wj*
\v 13 \wj None of you have¦64100 \+add ever\+add* gone¦64100 up¦64100 into¦64102 heaven¦64104, but I, the¦64107 son¦64113 of¦64115 humanity¦64115, have¦64111 come¦64111 down¦64111 from heaven¦64110.\wj*
\p
\v 14 “\wj Just like¦64122 Mosheh¦64123 lifted¦64124 up¦64124 that \+add bronze\+add* snake¦64126 \+add on a pole\+add* in¦64127 the¦64128 wilderness¦64129,\x + \xo 3:14: \xt Num 21:9.\x* it's¦64134 \+add also\+add* necessary¦64134 for the¦64136 son¦64137 of¦64139 humanity¦64139 to¦64133 be¦64133 lifted¦64133 up¦64133,\wj*\f + \fr 3:14 \ft lifted up / exalted: See https://bibleDifferences.net/2019/04/25/156-exulted\f*
\v 15 \wj so that¦64140 everyone¦64141 who believes¦64143 in¦64145 him¦64147 won't die, but \+add ≈will live¦64153\+add* forever¦64155.\wj*\f + \fr 3:15 \ft See http://bibleandtech.blogspot.com/2021/03/john-314-21-translation-and-commentary.html\f*
\v 16 \wj Because¦64157\wj*\f + \fr 3:16 \ft Sadly when older English translations use ‘For’ (following John Wycliffe's middle-English translation from Latin from the 1300's), it's quite easy to ignore what it's there for. The \+em OET\+em* uses the modern-English translation ‘Because’ which makes the connection to the previous verses (especially v14-15) clearer.\f* \wj in that same way, \+nd God¦64160\+nd* loves¦64158 \+add the people of\+add* the¦64161 world¦64162 enough to cause \+add &his\+add* only¦64168 son¦64165 to be born, and to give¦64170 him to the world, so¦64163 that¦64171 everyone¦64172 who believes¦64174 that won't¦64178 die¦64179, but¦64181 will \+add go on to\+add* \+add ≈live¦64183\+add* forever¦64184.\wj*
\p
\v 17 “\wj \+nd God¦64189\+nd* didn't¦64185 send¦64187 his¦64190 son¦64191 here to¦64193 condemn people, but¦64201 rather to save¦64203 them.\wj*
\v 18 \wj Anyone who trusts¦64209 in¦64210 \+add %me¦64211\+add* won't¦64212 be¦64213 condemned. However, anyone who doesn't believe¦64217 this has¦64219 already¦64218 been condemned because¦64220 he¦64222 rejected the¦64224 \+add ≈authority\+add* of¦64226 the¦64226 only¦64227 son¦64228 that \+nd God¦64230\+nd* fathered.\wj*
\v 19 \wj And¦64232 this¦64231 is¦64233 the¦64234 verdict: that¦64236 light¦64238 has¦64239 come¦64239 into¦64240 the¦64241 world¦64242, but¦64243 some people¦64247 love¦64244 the¦64250 darkness¦64251 more than¦64253 the¦64254 light¦64255 because¦64257 they do evil¦64260 things,\wj*
\v 20 \wj because¦64264 everyone¦64263 who does¦64267 evil¦64266 things hates¦64268 the¦64269 light¦64270 and¦64271 doesn't come¦64273 to¦64274 the¦64275 light¦64276 so that¦64277 their actions¦64282 won't be¦64279 exposed.\wj*
\v 21 \wj But¦64288 anyone who does what is right¦64291, comes¦64292 toward the¦64294 light¦64295 so that¦64296 their actions¦64300 can be¦64297 revealed¦64297 as being done with \nd God's¦64303\nd* help.\wj*”
\s1 Yohan approves of Yeshua's popularity
\rem /s1 Jesus and John the Baptist; John the Baptist Exalts Jesus; John the Baptist's Testimony About Jesus
\p
\v 22 After¦64308 this, \nd Yeshua¦64312\nd* and his¦64320 followers¦64319 went¦64310 down to¦64321 Yudea, and¦64326 stayed¦64328 there¦64327 and¦64331 immersed¦64332 some believers.
\v 23 Yohan¦64337 was¦64333 also¦64335 immersing¦64338 people at Aenon¦64340 near¦64341 Salim¦64344 because¦64345 there was plenty of water¦64346 there¦64349 and people would come \add to him\add* to get immersed¦64353.
\v 24 (At this point in time, Yohan¦64362 had not¦64354 yet¦64354 been¦64357 put in¦64358 prison¦64360.)\x + \xo 3:24: \xt Mat 14:3; Mrk 6:17; Luk 3:19-20.\x*
\v 25 Then a¦64366 debate¦64366 about¦64376 purification¦64377 started between Yohan's¦64372 followers¦64370 and a¦64374 religious leader.\f + \fr 3:25 \ft https://www.billmounce.com/monday-with-mounce/what-does-the-word-%E2%80%9Cjew%E2%80%9D-mean-you-john-3-25\f*
\v 26 \add ≈So¦64378\add* some people went¦64380 to¦64381 Yohan¦64383 and¦64384 said¦64385, “Teacher, that man that came¦64380 to¦64386 you¦64391 across the¦64393 river and that you¦64397 testified¦64398 about¦64396, now \em he's\em* immersing¦64402 people and¦64403 so they're all¦64404 going to¦64406 him¦64407.”
\p
\v 27 “None of us get¦64415 anything if¦64421 it's¦64424 not being given¦64426 from¦64428 heaven¦64430,” Yohan¦64409 answered¦64408.
\v 28 “You¦64432 yourselves¦64431 know that¦64435 I¦64436 said¦64436 that I'm¦64441 not¦64439 the¦64442 \nd messiah¦64443\nd*,\x + \xo 3:28: \xt Yhn 1:20.\x* but¦64444 rather the \nd one¦64443\nd* coming before¦64448 him.
\v 29 It's the¦64450 groom that has¦64451 the¦64452 bride¦64454—the best man is¦64469 happy because¦64470 he sees that the groom¦64474 is happy. So¦64476 I'm \add actually\add* completely happy with all this¦64475.
\v 30 It's¦64484 right¦64484 and proper that¦64482 he should increase¦64485 and I should fade out.”
\rem /s1 He Who Comes from Heaven; The One Who Comes from Heaven
\p
\v 31 “The¦64489 one who came¦64491 down from¦64490 heaven is¦64494 greater than¦64500 any of us. We came from¦64503 this world¦64505 and¦64507 speak¦64511 in our earthly¦64510 ways. The¦64512 one who came¦64517 down from¦64514 heaven¦64516 is¦64520 greater than any of us.
\v 32 He¦64528 explains about¦64532 what¦64522 he's¦64524 seen¦64524 and¦64525 heard¦64526, but¦64529 \add #people\add* don't believe him.
\v 33 Anyone who does believe him¦64537, confirms that¦64543 \nd God¦64545\nd* is¦64547 true¦64546.
\v 34 The¦64551 one that \nd God¦64552\nd* sent¦64550 tells us \nd God's¦64556\nd* words¦64554, because¦64559 \add @God¦64563\add* doesn't ration \add &his¦64566\add* \nd spirit¦64567\nd*.
\v 35 The¦64568 father¦64569 loves¦64570 the¦64571 son¦64572 and¦64573 has¦64575 \add ≈put him¦64580 in¦64577 charge of¦64580\add* everything.\x + \xo 3:35: \xt Mat 11:27; Luk 10:22.\x*
\v 36 Anyone who believes¦64583 \add &God's¦64585\add* son¦64586 \add ≈will live\add* forever¦64590, but¦64592 anyone who disobeys the¦64594 son¦64595 won't¦64596 be¦64598 seeing¦64598 life¦64599, but¦64600 will feel \nd God's¦64604\nd* severe¦64602 anger¦64602 \add instead\add*.”
\c 4
\s1 Yeshua chats with a woman at the well
\rem /s1 Jesus Talks With a Samaritan Woman; Jesus and the Samaritan Woman; Jesus and the Woman of Samaria
\p
\v 1 When¦64609 \nd Yeshua¦64620\nd* \add ≈found¦64611 out\add* that¦64615 the¦64617 Pharisee¦64618 party¦64618 knew¦64611 that¦64619 he was¦64623 gaining and¦64624 immersing¦64625 more¦64621 followers¦64622 than¦64626 Yohan¦64627 had,
\v 2 (although actually it wasn't \nd Yeshua¦64630\nd* himself¦64631 that was¦64634 immersing¦64634 them, but¦64635 his¦64638 apprentices¦64637 that were doing it),
\v 3 he¦64639 left¦64639 Yudea¦64641 and¦64643 went¦64644 back¦64645 up to¦64646 Galilee¦64648.
\v 4 On the way up, he decided to¦64652 go¦64652 through Shomron¦64655 \add !(Samaria¦64655)\add*.
\p
\v 5 By choosing that route, they came¦64656 to¦64658 a¦64659 town¦64659 in Shomron¦64661 called¦64662 Sukar¦64663, which¦64667 was near¦64664 the¦64665 place¦64666 that¦64667 the¦64671 \add patriarch\add* Yosef¦64672 had inherited from his¦64675 father Yacob¦64670,\x + \xo 4:5: \xt Gen 33:19; Josh 24:32.\x*
\v 6 and¦64677 ‘Yacob's¦64681 well’ was¦64676 there¦64678. \nd Yeshua¦64684\nd* was tired¦64685 from¦64686 all the¦64687 walking and was¦64689 sitting¦64689 by the¦64693 well¦64694 around¦64699 midday.
\p
\v 7 A¦64705 woman¦64705 came¦64703 from the¦64707 town to¦64709 get water¦64710 from the¦64713 well, and \nd Yeshua¦64714\nd* asked¦64711 her¦64712 for a drink¦64717
\v 8 since¦64719 his¦64721 followers¦64720 had¦64722 gone¦64722 into¦64723 the¦64724 town¦64725 to buy¦64728 some lunch.
\p
\v 9 The woman¦64733 said¦64729 to¦64731 him¦64731, “You're a Jew. How¦64736 come you're¦64737 asking¦64744 me¦64742 for a¦64747 drink¦64743 when I'm from¦64749 Shomron¦64749?” (Jews¦64754 don't¦64751 \add normally\add* associate¦64753 with anyone from Shomron¦64756.)\x + \xo 4:9: \xt Ezr 4:1-5; Neh 4:1-2.\x*
\p
\v 10 \nd Yeshua¦64759\nd* answered¦64757, “\wj If¦64763 you'd¦64764 recognised¦64764 \nd God's¦64768\nd* gift¦64766 and¦64769 who¦64770 it is¦64771 who's asking¦64773 you¦64774 for a drink¦64777, you¦64778 would¦64779 have asked \+add %me¦64781\+add* and¦64782 \+add %I¦64783\+add* would¦64784 have given¦64783 you¦64785 \+em living¦64787\+em* water¦64786 \+add to drink\+add*.\wj*”
\p
\v 11 But the¦64791 woman¦64793 \add ≈countered\add*, “Mister¦64794, you¦64798 don't even have¦64798 \add rope and\add* a bucket¦64797 to reach the water in the deep¦64803 well¦64801. How then could you¦64810 get ‘living¦64817 water¦64815’?
\v 12 I doubt that you're¦64819 greater¦64820 than¦64820 our¦64825 ancestor Yacob¦64826 who¦64828 made this well¦64833 for us¦64831 and¦64836 drank¦64841 this water along with his¦64845 children¦64844 and¦64846 his¦64849 animals¦64848.”
\p
\v 13 \nd Yeshua¦64852\nd* \add ≈responded\add*, “\wj Everyone¦64857 who drinks¦64859 this¦64863 water¦64862 will¦64864 get thirsty¦64864 again¦64865,\wj*
\v 14 \wj but¦64868 anyone¦64866 who drinks¦64871 the water that I give them will find a¦64899 well springing¦64901 up¦64901 inside them—springing into¦64902 eternal¦64904 life¦64903.\wj*”
\p
\v 15 So the¦64908 woman¦64909 said¦64905, “Okay, then. Give¦64911 me some of that¦64913 water¦64915 so that¦64916 I¦64918 won't¦64917 get thirsty¦64918 and won't have to keep coming out here¦64926 to¦64927 the well.”
\p
\v 16 \add @Yeshua¦64928\add* said¦64928, “\wj First, go¦64933 and get your¦64938 husband¦64937 and¦64939 then come¦64940 back here¦64941.\wj*”
\p
\v 17 “\add Actually,\add* I¦64951 don't¦64950 have¦64951 a¦64952 husband¦64952!” she \add ≈retorted\add*.
\p “\wj True enough—indeed you don't,\wj*” \nd Yeshua¦64956\nd* said¦64958.
\v 18 “\wj You've¦64967 had¦64967 five¦64964 husbands¦64966 and¦64968 you're¦64971 not¦64972 married to the man you're¦64974 living with, so what you¦64979 said¦64979 was true¦64978.\wj*”
\p
\v 19 “Mister¦64985, I¦64986 can see that¦64987 you're¦64990 a¦64988 prophet¦64988,” the¦64983 woman¦64984 \add ≈reacted\add*.
\v 20 “Our¦64993 ancestors¦64992 worshipped¦64999 on¦64994 this¦64998 mountain¦64997, but¦65000 you¦65001 Jews claim that¦65003 people should only worship there in¦65004 Yerushalem¦65005.”
\p
\v 21 Then \nd Yeshua¦65016\nd* told¦65013 her¦65014, “\wj You need to¦65014 believe¦65018 that I was sent from God, woman¦65021, because¦65022 a day is¦65023 coming¦65023 when¦65026 everyone¦65038 will be¦65038 worshipping¦65038 him neither¦65027 on¦65028 this¦65032 mountain¦65031, nor¦65035 in¦65036 Yerushalem¦65037.\wj*
\v 22 \wj You¦65041 people in Shomron don't¦65044 even know¦65045 who you worship, but we do, because¦65050 people will be¦65056 saved by means of¦65053 us Jews¦65055.\wj*
\v 23 \wj But¦65057 a time¦65059 is¦65058 coming¦65058, starting even now¦65061, when¦65063 the¦65064 true¦65065 worshippers¦65066 will¦65067 be¦65067 worshipping¦65067 the¦65068 father¦65069 in¦65070 spirit¦65071 and¦65072 truth¦65073, because¦65075 those are the¦65076 ones that he is¦65079 wanting¦65079 to worship him¦65082.\wj*
\v 24 \wj \+nd God¦65088\+nd* \+nd is¦65088\+nd* \+nd spirit¦65086\+nd*, and¦65090 the¦65091 ones worshipping him¦65093 must worship in¦65094 spirit¦65095 and¦65096 total honesty.\wj*”
\p
\v 25 \nd The¦65104\nd* woman¦65105 said¦65102, “I'm¦65106 aware that¦65108 the¦65109 messiah¦65109 is¦65110 coming¦65110—\add &God's¦65113\add* \nd chosen¦65113 one¦65113\nd*. Whenever¦65114 he¦65117 appears, he'll teach us¦65119 everything.”
\p
\v 26 “\wj \+em I¦65126 am¦65127\+em* the¦65124 messiah,\wj*” \nd Yeshua¦65125\nd* responded¦65122. “\wj Yes, he's¦65127 speaking¦65129 to¦65130 you¦65130!\wj*”
\rem /s1 The Disciples Rejoin Jesus
\p
\v 27 After¦65132 this¦65134, his¦65139 followers¦65138 arrived¦65136 back, and¦65140 they¦65141 were¦65141 astounded¦65141 that¦65143 he¦65146 was¦65146 speaking¦65146 with¦65144 a¦65145 woman¦65145. However¦65149 no¦65148 one¦65148 dared ask¦65151 her, “What¦65154 are¦65155 you¦65155 after?” Or¦65156 to ask him, “Why¦65157 are¦65158 you¦65158 talking¦65158 with¦65159 her¦65160?”
\p
\v 28 So¦65162 the¦65169 woman¦65170 left¦65161 her¦65167 water jar there, and¦65171 went¦65172 back into¦65173 the¦65174 town¦65175 where she¦65177 told¦65177 the¦65178 people¦65179,
\v 29 “Come¦65180 and see¦65181 a¦65182 man¦65182 who¦65183 knew as¦65188 much¦65188 about me as¦65188 I¦65189 know myself! He must be¦65193 the¦65194 \nd messiah¦65195\nd*!”
\v 30 So they¦65197 went¦65197 out from the¦65200 town¦65201 to¦65204 go and¦65202 see Yeshua.
\p
\v 31 Meanwhile¦65210, Yeshua's followers¦65214 encouraged him¦65212, “Teacher, here, eat¦65218.”
\p
\v 32 But¦65220 he¦65219 said¦65221, “\wj I've¦65223 had¦65225 food¦65224 to¦65226 eat¦65226 that¦65227 you¦65228 don't¦65229 know¦65230 about.\wj*”
\p
\v 33 This made \add &his¦65237\add* followers¦65238 ask¦65231 each other, “Did you see anyone¦65242 bring¦65243 him¦65244 something¦65244 to¦65245 eat¦65245?”
\p
\v 34 “\wj Obeying \+add @God¦65250\+add* who¦65253 sent¦65259 me is like food¦65251 to me¦65260, and¦65261 I¦65262 plan to finish¦65262 his¦65263 work¦65265,\wj*” \nd Yeshua¦65249\nd* explained.
\v 35 “\wj Don't¦65266 you¦65267 all¦65267 have a saying¦65268 about needing to wait four¦65271 months¦65271 for a harvest¦65276? But I'm¦65279 telling¦65279 you that¦65269 you¦65280 all¦65280 should open your eyes¦65284 and¦65286 look¦65287 at the¦65288 fields¦65289, because¦65290 they're¦65292 already¦65295 lightening up¦65281 as harvest¦65294 time approaches.\wj*
\v 36 \wj The¦65297 harvester gets paid with a¦65299 harvest that will last forever¦65307 so that¦65308 the¦65310 ones who plant and¦65315 the¦65316 ones who harvest¦65317 can all celebrate.\wj*
\v 37 \wj There's truth in the¦65324 statement¦65325 that¦65329 one person plants and¦65334 a different¦65335 \+add >person\+add* harvests¦65337.\wj*
\v 38 \wj I've¦65338 sent¦65339 you¦65341 all¦65341 out¦65339 to¦65342 harvest¦65342 where you¦65345 haven't worked¦65346 before—others¦65348 did the¦65354 groundwork and¦65351 you¦65352 benefit from their¦65356 work¦65355.\wj*”
\rem /s1 Many Samaritans Believe
\p
\v 39 And¦65359 many¦65363 people of¦65367 Shomron¦65368 came out¦65358 of¦65358 that¦65362 town¦65361 and believed¦65364 that \add @Yeshua¦65366\add* is God because¦65369 the¦65372 woman¦65373 had told¦65376 them that¦65375 he¦65376 knew everything about her.
\v 40 So¦65384 when¦65382 \add *they\add* all came¦65386, they¦65391 asked¦65391 him¦65392 to¦65393 stay¦65393 in their town and¦65398 they stayed¦65399 on there¦65402 for a couple of days¦65404.
\p
\v 41 As a result of¦65411 his¦65414 teaching, many¦65407 more¦65408 believed¦65410
\v 42 so then they¦65421 told¦65421 the woman¦65419, “We¦65432 no¦65425 longer¦65425 believe¦65432 just¦65443 because¦65426 of¦65426 what you said¦65421, but now that¦65424 we've¦65436 heard¦65436 him for ourselves¦65433, we¦65440 can see that¦65441 he really is¦65445 the¦65447 saviour¦65448 of¦65449 the¦65449 world¦65450.”
\s1 Yeshua heals the official's son
\rem /s1 Jesus the giver of life; Jesus Returns to Galilee; Jesus Heals an Official's Son; Jesus Heals the Official's Son
\p
\v 43 After¦65453 \add &his¦65455\add* two¦65456 days¦65457 in \add @Shomron\add* \add !(Samaria)\add*, \add @Yeshua\add* continued on up to¦65462 Galilee¦65464.
\v 44 \nd He\nd* himself¦65465 had told them that¦65470 no prophet¦65471 gets honoured¦65476 in¦65472 his¦65473 own¦65474 home town.\x + \xo 4:44: \xt Mat 13:57; Mrk 6:4; Luk 4:24.\x*
\v 45 When¦65479 he¦65482 got to¦65483 Galilee¦65485, the¦65489 people accepted¦65487 him¦65488, having¦65492 seen¦65492 everything that he'd¦65496 done¦65496 at¦65500 the¦65501 feast¦65502 in Yerushalem¦65499 because¦65505 they¦65504 had also¦65503 been down there.\x + \xo 4:45: \xt Yhn 2:23.\x*
\rem /s1 Jesus Heals an Official's Son
\p
\v 46 So¦65516 he¦65514 went¦65514 again to¦65521 Cana¦65525 there in Galilee¦65528 where¦65529 he¦65530 had made¦65530 the¦65532 water¦65533 into wine¦65534.\x + \xo 4:46: \xt Yhn 2:1-11.\x* Now there was¦65536 a¦65538 royal¦65540 official¦65540 there, whose¦65541 son¦65543 in¦65545 Capernaum¦65546 was ill.
\v 47 When the official heard¦65548 that¦65549 \nd Yeshua¦65551\nd* was¦65552 coming¦65552 up from Yudea¦65556 to¦65557 Galilee¦65559, he went¦65560 and¦65565 asked¦65566 him if he¦65569 would come¦65569 and¦65571 heal¦65572 his¦65573 son¦65575 who was¦65576 dying¦65578.
\v 48 \nd Yeshua¦65582\nd* said¦65579 to¦65583 him¦65584, “\wj You¦65591 people won't¦65586 believe¦65594 unless you see¦65591 miracles¦65587 and¦65588 other marvels.\wj*”
\p
\v 49 But the¦65598 official¦65600 begged him¦65597, “Sir, please come¦65603 before¦65604 my¦65611 child¦65608 dies¦65605.”
\p
\v 50 “\wj Go back there and see,\wj*” \nd Yeshua¦65615\nd* responded¦65612. “\wj Your¦65619 son¦65618 will recover.\wj*”
\p The¦65623 man¦65624 believed¦65622 what \nd Yeshua¦65633\nd* had told¦65629 him¦65630, and¦65635 so he¦65636 started off.
\v 51 On his way, his slaves¦65644 met¦65646 him¦65648 and¦65650 reported¦65651 that¦65655 the¦65656 boy¦65658 was¦65661 alive¦65661 and well.
\p
\v 52 So¦65663 the¦65666 official asked them¦65670 what time it was that¦65672 he¦65674 got better¦65673, and they¦65676 replied¦65676 that¦65679 the¦65686 fever¦65687 had subsided around 1pm.
\v 53 The¦65690 father¦65691 knew¦65688 that¦65693 that¦65695 was¦65695 the¦65696 time¦65697 when \nd Yeshua¦65703\nd* had told¦65700 him¦65701 that his son¦65706 would recover, and as a result his whole¦65716 household¦65714 believed¦65710 \add that Yeshua came from God\add*.
\p
\v 54 This¦65717 was¦65717 the¦65722 second¦65722 miracle¦65723 that \nd Yeshua¦65727\nd* have done¦65724 after leaving Yudea¦65731 and going to¦65732 Galilee¦65734.
\c 5
\s1 Yeshua heals a man at the pool
\rem /s1 The Healing at the Pool; Jesus Heals on the Sabbath; Jesus Heals a Lame Man
\p
\v 1 After¦65735 all this, there¦65737 was¦65737 another Jewish feast¦65739, so¦65742 \nd Yeshua¦65745\nd* went¦65743 down to¦65746 Yerushalem¦65747.
\v 2 In¦65750 Yerushalem¦65752 at¦65754 the¦65755 Sheep¦65756 Gate¦65756, there's¦65748 the¦65751 Bethsaida¦65766 pool¦65757 that¦65758 has¦65770 five¦65768 alcoves
\v 3 and a large number of¦65778 sick, blind¦65780, lame¦65781, and paralysed¦65782 people¦65776 lie¦65774 there in them.
\v 4 ◘
\v 5 One man¦65825 had been there¦65826 for thirty-eight years¦65832,
\v 6 and when \nd Yeshua¦65842\nd* noticed¦65839 him and¦65845 knew¦65846 that¦65847 he'd¦65853 been¦65853 there for so long, he¦65854 asked¦65854, “\wj Do you¦65856 want¦65856 to¦65858 get¦65858 better?\wj*”
\p
\v 7 “Yes mister¦65869,” the¦65867 sick man¦65870 answered¦65864, “but when¦65875 the¦65877 water¦65878 starts moving, I¦65873 don't¦65872 have¦65873 a companion to lift me¦65882 into¦65883 the¦65884 pool¦65885, so someone else always get there before¦65893 me¦65895.”
\p
\v 8 Then \nd Yeshua¦65900\nd* said¦65897, “\wj Stand up and pick¦65904 up¦65904 your¦65907 bedroll and¦65908 start walking¦65909.\wj*”
\v 9 The¦65915 man¦65916 immediately¦65911 stood up, picked¦65921 up¦65921 his¦65925 gear, and¦65926 started to walk¦65927.
\p However, this was¦65929 the¦65931 weekly rest¦65931 day¦65935.
\v 10 So¦65937 the¦65939 religious leaders said¦65936 to¦65941 the¦65941 man, “Hey! It's¦65944 against the¦65943 law for¦65948 you¦65948 to¦65949 carry¦65949 your¦65953 bedding¦65952 on the¦65951 rest¦65943 day¦65943!”\x + \xo 5:10: \xt Neh 13:19; Jer 17:21.\x*
\p
\v 11 But¦65956 the¦65955 man¦65955 answered¦65957, “The¦65960 man who made¦65961 me¦65962 better told¦65966 me to pick¦65967 up¦65967 my bedroll and¦65974 start walking¦65975.”
\p
\v 12 “Oh. Who¦65980 was¦65981 it that¦65984 told¦65985 you¦65986 to¦65986 take¦65987 that stuff and¦65992 start walking¦65993?”
\p
\v 13 But¦65996 the¦65995 man who had¦65997 been¦65997 healed¦65997 didn't¦65999 even know¦66000 who¦66001 it was¦66002, because¦66005 \nd Yeshua¦66007\nd* had quickly left when a¦66010 crowd¦66010 had formed.
\p
\v 14 Later¦66016 on, \nd Yeshua¦66022\nd* found¦66018 the man in¦66025 the¦66026 temple¦66027 and¦66028 told¦66029 him¦66031, “\wj Look¦66032, you're¦66034 better now so don't go on sinning¦66036, because you don't want anything worse¦66039 to happen¦66043 to¦66041 you¦66041.\wj*”
