\p
\v 18 Because¦66106 of¦66106 this¦66107, the¦66113 leaders became determined that he must be¦66110 put to¦66117 death—not just because¦66118 he¦66121 broke¦66121 the rules for the rest¦66123 day¦66123, but¦66124 most of all because he¦66128 was¦66128 calling¦66128 \nd God¦66131\nd* his own¦66127 father¦66126, thus making¦66134 himself¦66133 equal¦66132 \nd to¦66136 God¦66136\nd*!
\s1 Authority over life is given to the son
\rem /s1 The Authority of the Son
\p
\v 19 So¦66139 \nd Yeshua¦66141\nd* responded to¦66146 them¦66146, “\wj I¦66152 want to¦66153 tell you¦66153 all¦66153 something: The¦66156 son¦66157 can't¦66154 initiate anything¦66173 by himself¦66164. He can only¦66169 do what he sees¦66174 \+add &his¦66176\+add* father¦66177 doing¦66178, because¦66181 whatever¦66180 \+add &his\+add* father is¦66185 doing¦66185, he also¦66189 does¦66193 things like that¦66184.\wj*
\v 20 \wj You see, the¦66195 father¦66197 loves¦66199 \+add &his¦66200\+add* son¦66201 and¦66202 shows¦66204 him¦66205 everything that¦66206 he's doing¦66209. In fact, he'll¦66215 be¦66215 showing¦66215 him even greater¦66212 things than¦66212 what he's done¦66219 already, so that¦66220 you¦66221 all¦66221 will be¦66222 amazed¦66222.\wj*
\v 21 \wj Because¦66227 the¦66228 father¦66229 brings the¦66233 dead¦66234 back to life, giving¦66238 them new life¦66238, so¦66239 too the¦66241 son¦66242 can give¦66245 life¦66245 to anyone who¦66243 he wants.\wj*
\v 22 \wj The¦66249 father¦66250 won't¦66246 be¦66251 judging¦66251 anyone¦66252, but¦66253 has¦66257 already given¦66257 that task to¦66259 the¦66259 son¦66260,\wj*
\v 23 \wj so that¦66261 the people might¦66263 honour¦66263 the¦66264 son¦66265 like¦66266 they¦66267 honour¦66267 the¦66268 father¦66269. But anyone who is not¦66271 honouring¦66272 the¦66273 son¦66274, is¦66276 \+add also\+add* dishonouring the¦66277 father¦66278 who sent¦66280 him¦66281.\wj*
\p
\v 24 “\wj I¦66284 assure you¦66285 that¦66286 anyone who hears¦66291 my¦66290 message¦66289 and¦66292 believes¦66293 that I was sent¦66295 by \+add @God¦66296\+add*, \+add ≈will live\+add* forever¦66299 and¦66300 will not¦66303 be condemned, but¦66307 has¦66308 moved from death¦66311 into¦66312 life¦66314.\wj*
\v 25 \wj I¦66317 can also assure you¦66318 that¦66319 a time¦66321 is¦66320 coming¦66320, and¦66322 in fact is¦66324 here already, when¦66325 the¦66326 dead¦66327 will¦66330 be¦66330 hearing¦66330 the¦66331 voice¦66332 of¦66333 \nd God's¦66336\nd* son¦66334 and¦66337 that voice will¦66341 \+add ≈bring them back to life¦66341\+add*.\wj*
\v 26 \wj As¦66342 the¦66345 father¦66346 is¦66349 the source of life¦66350, he¦66359 gave¦66359 the power of giving life¦66360 to¦66357 the¦66357 son¦66358\wj*
\v 27 \wj and¦66365 gave¦66369 him the authority¦66367 to¦66370 be¦66374 the final \+add ≈judge¦66372\+add*, because¦66375 he¦66378 is¦66378 the¦66376 son¦66376 of¦66377 humanity¦66377.\wj*
\v 28 \wj Don't¦66379 be¦66380 surprised at¦66381 this¦66381, because¦66382 a time¦66384 is¦66383 coming¦66383 when everyone¦66387 in¦66390 \+add &their¦66391\+add* graves¦66393 will¦66398 be¦66398 hearing¦66398 his¦66401 voice¦66400,\wj*
\v 29 \wj and¦66402 the¦66406 ones having¦66409 done what is good¦66408 will¦66404 be¦66404 given new life¦66412, and¦66415 the ones having¦66418 done¦66418 what is evil¦66417 will be condemned.\wj*”\x + \xo 5:29: \xt Dan 12:2.\x*
\s1 The unbelief of the religious leaders
\rem /s1 Witnesses to Jesus
\p
\v 30 Yeshua continued explaining to the religious leaders, “\wj I¦66426 don't¦66423 do¦66427 anything in isolation. Whenever I¦66436 hear¦66436 from him, only then do I¦66437 judge¦66437 and¦66438 my¦66442 judgement¦66440 is¦66444 correct and impartial because¦66445 I'm¦66447 not¦66446 imposing \+em my¦66451\+em* desires, but¦66452 the¦66454 desire of¦66456 the¦66456 one who sent¦66457 me¦66458.\wj*
\rem /s1 Testimonies About Jesus; Witnesses to Jesus
\p
\v 31 “\wj If¦66460 I¦66461 just testified¦66462 about¦66463 myself¦66464, my¦66467 testimony¦66466 would not¦66468 be correct or even valid¦66470.\wj*
\v 32 \wj However it's another¦66471 one that's testifying¦66474 about¦66475 me¦66476, and¦66477 I¦66478 know¦66478 that¦66480 his testimony¦66484 about¦66488 me¦66489 is¦66482 true¦66481.\wj*
\v 33 \wj You¦66490 sent¦66491 people out¦66491 to¦66492 question Yohan¦66493 and¦66494 his testimony¦66495 was true¦66497.\wj*\x + \xo 5:33: \xt Yhn 1:19-27; 3:27-30.\x*
\v 34 \wj but¦66499 I¦66498 don't¦66500 even need any testimony¦66506 that¦66511 comes from¦66501 people, because I¦66510 am¦66510 teaching¦66510 you¦66512 how to be¦66513 saved¦66513.\wj*
\v 35 \wj \+add @Yohan\+add* was¦66515 a bright and¦66520 shining¦66521 light¦66531 and¦66523 you¦66522 appreciated it for¦66526 a¦66527 short time¦66527.\wj*
\v 36 \wj But¦66534 I¦66533 have¦66535 a stronger testimony¦66537 than¦66539 Yohan's¦66542 because¦66544 the father¦66552 has¦66547 entrusted works to¦66550 me¦66550 to complete¦66554, and which¦66560 I'm¦66562 \+add already\+add* doing¦66562 and which \+add clearly\+add* show¦66563 that¦66567 the¦66568 father¦66569 sent¦66571 me¦66570 here.\wj*
\v 37 \wj And¦66573 since he sent¦66575 me¦66576, he himself has¦66581 testified¦66581 about¦66582 me¦66583.\x + \xo 5:37: \xt Mat 3:17; Mrk 1:11; Luk 3:22.\x* You¦66590 people have¦66590 never listened¦66590 to his¦66586 voice¦66585, nor¦66591 have¦66594 you¦66594 ever¦66588 seen¦66594 him¦66593!\wj*
\v 38 \wj And¦66595 his¦66598 way of thinking is¦66600 \+add obviously\+add* not¦66599 in¦66602 your minds, because¦66605 you¦66611 don't¦66612 believe¦66613 the one that¦66609 he¦66607 sent¦66607.\wj*
\v 39 \wj You¦66614 look¦66614 in the¦66615 \+add Jewish\+add* scriptures¦66616 because¦66617 you¦66618 suppose¦66619 that they'll lead you to¦66625 eternal¦66624 life¦66623. Those¦66629 very scriptures testify¦66633 about¦66634 me¦66635 \+add coming\+add*,\wj*
\v 40 \wj yet you¦66638 \+add ^refuse\+add* to¦66639 come¦66639 to¦66640 me¦66641 in¦66642 order¦66642 to receive life¦66643.\wj*
\p
\v 41 “\wj I'm¦66651 not¦66650 getting¦66651 any praise from¦66647 people¦66648\wj*
\v 42 \wj but¦66652 I¦66653 do know¦66653 that¦66655 you people don't¦66662 \+add actually\+add* love¦66659 \+nd God¦66661\+nd* in¦66665 your hearts.\wj*
\v 43 \wj I¦66667 have¦66669 come¦66669 with my¦66675 father's¦66674 \+add ≈authority\+add* and¦66676 you¦66678 don't¦66677 accept¦66678 me¦66679, but if¦66680 someone came¦66682 claiming their own¦66687 \+add ≈authority\+add*, you'd¦66689 \+add happily\+add* accept¦66689 them.\wj*
\v 44 \wj How¦66690 \+em could¦66691\+em* you¦66692 possibly believe¦66693 when you just accept¦66698 acclamations from¦66696 each other, but don't¦66707 even seek¦66708 praise from¦66703 the¦66704 only¦66705 \+nd God¦66706\+nd*.\wj*
\v 45 \wj But don't¦66710 be¦66711 assuming that¦66712 I'll¦66713 be¦66714 accusing¦66714 you¦66715 all¦66715 \+add ≈in¦66718 front¦66718 of¦66718\+add* the¦66719 father¦66720. No, the¦66722 one who'll accuse¦66723 you¦66724 is¦66721 Mosheh¦66728 because he's the one that you're¦66731 hoping¦66732 to please.\wj*
\v 46 \wj The trouble is that¦66744 if¦66733 you¦66735 \+add actually\+add* believed¦66735 what Mosheh¦66736 wrote, you¦66737 would believe¦66737 me¦66739, because¦66741 \+add @Mosheh\+add* was writing¦66745 about¦66740 me¦66742.\wj*
\v 47 \wj But¦66748 since you¦66753 don't¦66752 \+add really\+add* believe¦66753 his writings¦66751, you're¦66759 not at all¦66759 likely to believe¦66759 me.\wj*”
\c 6
