\p
\v 30 “If so¦67421,” they¦67419 said¦67419, “what¦67423 miracle¦67428 will¦67426 you¦67427 do for us to see¦67432 so¦67433 that we¦67434 can believe¦67434 that you¦67435 \add came from God\add*? What¦67436 can \em you¦67437\em* do¦67437?
\v 31 Our¦67440 ancestors¦67439 ate¦67443 the¦67441 manna¦67442\f + \fr 6:31 \ft Manna was a word that meant ‘stuff’ and referred to some kind of flakes that regularly came down from the sky in the time of Mosheh and could be eaten as food.\f* out¦67452 in¦67444 the¦67445 wilderness¦67446, just like¦67447 Mosheh wrote¦67449, ‘He¦67455 gave¦67455 them bread¦67451 from the¦67453 sky¦67454 to¦67458 eat¦67458.’ ”\x + \xo 6:31: \xt Exo 16:4,15; Psa 78:24.\x*
