\v 8 \wj The ones who came¦71855 before¦71856 me¦71857 are¦71860 thieves¦71859 and¦71861 robbers¦71862, but¦71863 the¦71869 sheep¦71870 didn't¦71864 listen¦71865 to them¦71867.\wj*
\v 9 \wj \+em I¦71871 am¦71873\+em* the¦71874 entrance¦71875. Anyone¦71880 who comes¦71881 in¦71881 via me¦71877 will¦71882 be¦71882 saved¦71882, and¦71883 will¦71884 be¦71884 able to go in¦71884 and¦71885 out¦71886 and¦71887 find¦71889 pasture¦71888.\wj*
\v 10 \wj The¦71890 thief¦71892 only¦71895 comes¦71894 to steal¦71900 and¦71901 kill and¦71903 destroy¦71904, but I¦71905 came¦71907 so that¦71908 they¦71911 \+add ≈could¦71911 live¦71909\+add*, and¦71912 \+add ≈live\+add* a full life¦71909.\wj*
\p
\v 11 “\wj \+em I¦71916 am¦71917\+em* the good¦71922 shepherd¦71920\x + \xo 10:11: \xt Eze 34:11-16,23.\x*—the¦71925 good¦71926 shepherd¦71924 gives his¦71929 own life¦71928 for¦71932 the¦71933 sheep¦71934.\wj*\f + \fr 10:11 \ft See http://bibleandtech.blogspot.com/2021/04/john-1011-18-translations-and-notes-rcl.html\f*
\v 12 \wj The¦71935 paid worker is not even¦71939 the¦71942 shepherd¦71942, because the sheep¦71949 aren't¦71944 his¦71948 own¦71951 and if he sees¦71952 a wolf¦71954 coming¦71956 he just abandons¦71958 the¦71959 sheep¦71960 and¦71961 takes off and¦71963 the¦71964 wolf¦71965 scatters¦71969 the sheep and¦71968 snatches¦71966 some—\wj*
\v 13 \wj that's because¦71976 he's¦71979 just a¦71977 worker and¦71980 doesn't \+add really\+add* care¦71982 about¦71985 the¦71986 sheep¦71987.\wj*
